ds, the two are compared on the same servers and days, and the result is published both ways, with HISTOR's own misses.\n\n### ScraperWatch\n\nA daily diff of a fixed panel of about 3,000 remote endpoints. HISTOR compares each of their published days with its own reads, and ScraperWatch shows the result on its page under \"Outside check\". The first comparison found a robots.txt parsing limit on their side and a handshake regression on HISTOR's; both were fixed the same day.\n\nscraperwatch.com/mcp-changes\n/datasets/peers/scraperwatch/latest\n\n### heldfast\n\nAn open daily record of the tool definitions of the servers in the official MCP registry. Of the 23,190 servers both logs recorded on 26 October 2026, 21,215 had every field in both; on those, 97.9% of servers and 99.1% of tools were identical byte for byte, and each difference has a stated cause: package versions, read times, failed reads, a first page only, an older protocol.\n\ngithub.com/rufat325/heldfast\n/datasets/interop-digests-2026-10-31\n\nFor clients, registries and server authors\n\n## Use it\n\nBefore your agent trusts a server, send the tools it received. The answer is signed by the log's did:key and names the tree head it was given under.\n    \n    curl -sS https://histor.modelmarket.dev/api/v1/check \\\n      -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \\\n      -d '{\"endpoint\":\"https://example.com/mcp\",\"tools\":[ …tools/list result… ],\"contribute\":true}'\n    # -> {\"type\":\"histor.check/v1\",\"match\":\"same\"|\"different\"|\"previously-observed\"|…,\n    #     \"observed\":{\"unchangedSince\":\"…\",\"changes\":0}, \"patternScan\":{…}, \"signature\":{…}}\n    \n    # README badge for your server\n    [![MCP tool defs](https://histor.modelmarket.dev/badge/<id>.svg)](https://histor.modelmarket.dev/s/<id>)\n    \n    # Atom feed of every observed change\n    https://histor.modelmarket.dev/feed.xml\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n (https://glama.ai/mcp/servers/alexar76/histor/tree)\nciteturn23search2 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 3 weeks ago;     > 💬 **[Issues](https://github.com/alexar76/histor/issues)** · **[Pull requests](https://github.com/alexar76/histor/pulls)** both welcome. ...     | [AIMarket Hub](https://modelmarket.dev) | lists `histor.check@v1` in the catalogue |\n\n## histor\n\n\nSecurityObservability\n\nby alexar76\n\nOverviewSchemaSourceRelated ServersDiscussionsAdmin\n\nPython\n\nRemote\n\n  * histor\n\n  * deploy\n\n  * docs\n\n  * .github\n\n  * histor\n\n  * sandbox\n\n  * scanner\n\n  * scripts\n\n  * tests\n\n\nREADME.md\n    \n    `<!-- aicom-mirror-notice -->\n    > **🔄 Synced from a monorepo — but with a live history.** `histor` mirrors the\n    > canonical AI-Factory monorepo. History here is append-only (no force-push).\n    > **Pull requests are welcome** — merged PRs are imported back into the monorepo\n    > and re-synced here, so your contribution becomes canonical.\n    > 💬 **[Issues](https://github.com/alexar76/histor/issues)** · **[Pull requests](https://github.com/alexar76/histor/pulls)** both welcome.\n    \n    # HISTOR\n    \n    <!-- aicom-readme-badges -->\n    <p align=\"center\">\n      <a href=\"https://github.com/alexar76/histor/actions/workflows/ci.yml\"><img src=\"https://github.com/alexar76/histor/actions/workflows/ci.yml/badge.svg\" alt=\"CI\" /></a>\n      <a href=\"https://github.com/alexar76/histor/actions/workflows/pages.yml\"><img src=\"https://github.com/alexar76/histor/actions/workflows/pages.yml/badge.svg\" alt=\"Pages\" /></a>\n      <a href=\"https://histor.modelmarket.dev/\"><img src=\"https://img.shields.io/website?url=https%3A%2F%2Fhistor.modelmarket.dev%2Fhealth&label=live&up_message=up&down_message=down\" alt=\"Live service\" /></a>\n      <a href=\"https://histor.modelmarket.dev/log\"><img src=\"https://img.shields.io/endpoint?url=https%3A%2F%2Fhistor.modelmarket.dev%2Fapi%2Fv1%2Fbadges%2Flog\" alt=\"Labels in the log (live)\" /></a>\n      <img src=\"https://img.shields.io/badge/docs-EN%20RU%20ES%20FR%20ZH-9c70ff\" alt=\"Documentation in 5 languages\" />\n      <a href=\"https://github.com/alexar76/histor/blob/main/LICENSE\"><img src=\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/alexar76/histor/refs/heads/main/docs/badges/license.svg\" alt=\"License: MIT\" /></a>\n    </p>\n    <!-- /aicom-readme-badges -->\n    \n    <p align=\"center\">\n      <strong>HISTOR</strong> (ἵστωρ, “the one who knows because they saw”) — a public transparency log of MCP tool definitions<br>\n      What every remote MCP endpoint in the official registry advertised · when it changed · signed, appended, auditable\n    </p>\n    \n    <p align=\"center\">\n      <a href=\"README.md\"><b>English</b></a> ·\n      <a href=\"README.ru.md\">Русский</a> ·\n      <a href=\"README.es.md\">Español</a> ·\n      <a href=\"README.fr.md\">Français</a> ·\n      <a href=\"README.zh.md\">中文</a>\n    </p>\n    \n    > [WARDEN quality cycle: MOMUS → AI-Factory → SKOPOS → shared node agent → deployment](../momus/docs/quality-cycle.md).\n    \n    **Live:** [histor.modelmarket.dev](https://histor.modelmarket.dev) ·\n    **Landing:** [alexar76.github.io/histor](https://alexar76.github.io/histor/) ·\n    **Capabilities:** `histor.check@v1` · `histor.server@v1` · `histor.changes@v1` ·\n    **Port:** `9490`\n    \n    ## The problem, in one paragraph\n    \n    An MCP server can pass your review with harmless tool descriptions and change them later —\n    a new sentence in a description is all a prompt injection needs, and your client will pass it\n    to the model without asking you again. MCP has no content addressing for tool definitions, the\n    official registry verifies namespaces rather than contents, and a scanner on your laptop sees\n    only what the server shows your laptop. HISTOR is the missing public memory: it records what\n    each server advertised, signs it, and tells anyone who asks whether what they received is what\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nWARDEN — MCP Security Firewall - Odel Module Marketplace (https://odel.app/modules/alexar76/warden)\nciteturn23search3 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 3 weeks ago; To avoid repeated cold `npx` starts, install globally with `npm install -g @aimarket/warden@0.16.0`, then use `warden-mcp`. ...     io.github.alexar76/warden\n## Protect Claude Desktop or Cursor with one wrapper\n\nUse 0.8.2 or later: 0.8.0 and 0.8.1 let a wrapped server forge the reply to the client's own `tools/list` (CHANGELOG). From source, `node /absolute/path/warden/dist/mcp-server.js wrap ...` works the same. Adding WARDEN as a separate MCP server does not inspect other servers. Tested end to end with the MCP TypeScript SDK and fixture servers; runs in Claude Desktop and Cursor themselves are not yet recorded (release validation). Replace each protected server’s command with `wrap`:\n\njson Copy\n    \n    `{\n      \"mcpServers\": {\n        \"filesystem\": {\n          \"command\": \"npx\",\n          \"args\": [\"-y\", \"@aimarket/warden@0.16.0\", \"wrap\", \"--id\", \"filesystem\", \"--\",\n                   \"npx\", \"-y\", \"@modelcontextprotocol/server-filesystem\", \"/Users/me/docs\"]\n        }\n      }\n    }\n    `\n\nFor explicit first-contact review, add `--require-approval` to `wrap`. It withholds new definitions until `warden-mcp pins approve --id filesystem` in an operator terminal, then rejects any changed field or launch identity. ## Development\n\nbash Copy\n    \n    `npm install && npm run build && npm test   # 443 tests\n    `\n\n`test/packaging.test.ts` is what keeps the headline honest: it fails if an npm runtime dependency appears, if any source file imports outside the package (except `node:` builtins), or if the entry point stops exporting the enforcement surface. `test/mcp-server.test.ts` is the Glama health check: `initialize` + `tools/list` + a `tools/call`.\n\nUsed by ARGUS (the reference host), MOMUS (the publisher side), and the AICOM MCP-security course.\n\nMIT © AICOM (alexar76)\n\n## Checked by Odel\n\n  * Registry verified the namespace io.github.alexar76\n  * Repository reachable, not archived\n\n### Assessed by AI Jev\n\nHarmful\n    \n    5%\nFirst-party\n    \n    33%\nHigh impact\n    \n    9%\nAdult content\n    \n    1%\n\nRead from the listing and README on 15 Oct 2026. AI can make mistakes: a guide, not a check.\n\n## Requirements\n\nRuns\n    On your machine\n\nSign-in\n    npm\n\nCredentials\n    None asked\n\nClients\n    Any MCP client\n\n  * @aimarket/warden@0.16.0 npm 830 a week\n\n## Details\n\nVersion\n    0.16.0\n\nUpdated\n    14 Oct 2026\n\nRepo created\n    24 Aug 2026\n\nLicense\n    MIT\n\nLanguage\n    TypeScript\n\nGitHub\n    0 stars · 0 forks · 0 issues\n\nRegistry name\n    io.github.alexar76/warden\n\n  * alexar76/warden\n  * warden.modelmarket.dev\n  * Registry listing--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nEthereum Blocks #23512760 | Etherscan (https://etherscan.io/block/23512760)\nciteturn23search4 [wordlim: 200] Published: 1.1 years ago; Crawled: 5 months ago; #23512760\n\n# Block\n\n#23512760\n\nMEV Block\n\nEigenPhi\n\nBlock Height:\n\n23512760\n\nStatus:\n\nFinalized\n\nTimestamp:\n\nOct-05-2025 04:27:59 PM +UTC\n\n[Input]Oct-05-2025 04:27:59 PM +UTC\n\nTime Formats\n\nUTC\n\nLocal\n\nUnix Timestamp\n\nProposed On:\n\nBlock proposed on slot 12738138 , epoch 398066\n\nTransactions:\n\n234 transactions and 146 contract internal transactions in this block\n\nWithdrawals:\n\n16 withdrawals in this block\n\n* * *\n\nFee Recipient:\n\nTitan Builder in 12 secs\n\nBlock Reward:\n\n0.014210696968245287 ETH (0 + 0.01702880315945588 - 0.002818106191210593)\n\nTotal Difficulty:\n\n0\n\nSize:\n\n148,953 bytes\n\n* * *\n\nGas Used:\n\n21,735,897 (48.49%)\n\nGas Limit:\n\n44,823,542\n\nBase Fee Per Gas:\n\n0.000000000129652169 ETH (0.129652169 Gwei)\n\nBurnt Fees:\n\n🔥 0.002818106191210593 ETH\n\nExtra Data: